.TH BALLSIM_V2 1 2026-10-30 "ballsim 2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ballsim_v2, ballsim \- interactive 2D hard-sphere gas simulation in a
parabolic vessel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ballsim_v2
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-substeps\fR \fIK\fR]
[\fB\-\-passes\fR \fIP\fR]
[\fB\-\-threads\fR \fIT\fR]
[\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIS\fR]
.br
.B ballsim_v2
.B \-\-bench
\fIN\fR \fISTEPS\fR
.br
.B ballsim_v2
.B \-\-screenshot
\fIFILE\fR \fIK\fR
.br
.B ballsim_v2
.B \-\-write\-config
[\fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B ballsim
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-write\-config\fR [\fIFILE\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ballsim_v2
is a real-time molecular dynamics simulation of a two-species hard-sphere gas
under gravity, confined by a parabolic (or flat) floor, vertical walls and a
ceiling that can oscillate as a piston.  It displays the particles, a stats
panel with live sliders for every physical parameter, and an analysis panel
showing equipartition between species, the Boltzmann H-function, the
barometric density profile, wall pressure and the hard-disc equation of
state, a P\-V loop for the piston, the mean-squared displacement of the heavy
particles, and the mean free path compared with Enskog theory.
.PP
Two engines are provided.
.B ballsim
(v1) is event-driven: every collision time is solved analytically and the
dynamics are exact, but detection is O(N\(S2) and the particle count is
limited to 500.
.B ballsim_v2
integrates with a fixed timestep and a cell list, resolves overlaps with
impulses, and runs the collision pass in parallel with OpenMP; it handles up
to 5000 particles.  Position corrections are made energy-consistent, so the
measured energy drift is about 0.002\ % over 40\ s at N\ =\ 1000.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Load parameters from
.IR FILE .
Without this option the file is searched for as described under
.BR FILES .
.TP
.BR \-\-write\-config " [" \fIFILE\fR ]
Write a config file containing the built-in defaults (default name
.IR ballsim_v2.cfg )
and exit.  Use this to obtain a template to edit.
.TP
.BI \-\-bench " N STEPS"
Headless benchmark: run
.I STEPS
fixed timesteps of 1/120\ s with
.I N
particles, no window, and print throughput, energy drift, collision rate,
compressibility, mean free path and residual overlap.
.TP
.BI \-\-screenshot " FILE K"
Run
.I K
timesteps offscreen, render one frame to
.I FILE
(BMP) and exit.  Useful for documentation and for checking the layout on a
headless machine.
.TP
.BI \-\-substeps " K"
Verlet sub-steps per 1/120\ s outer step (default 8).  Lowering to 4 roughly
doubles throughput at the cost of larger residual overlaps; energy drift is
unaffected.
.TP
.BI \-\-passes " P"
Overlap-resolution passes per sub-step (default 4).
.TP
.BI \-\-threads " T"
Number of OpenMP threads (default: all cores).  Ignored in a build without
OpenMP.
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " S"
Seed for the random number generator (default: current time).  Benchmarks
and screenshots are reproducible with a fixed seed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B M
Reset, monoenergetic: every particle gets kinetic energy
\(12\(mu\fImono_speed\fR\(S2 with a random direction.
.TP
.B R
Reset with random speeds.
.TP
.B C
Cycle the colour mode: SPECIES, SPEED, KE, HEIGHT, RAINBOW.
.TP
.B T
Reset the mean-squared-displacement reference and the tracer trail.
.TP
.B V
Start or stop MP4 recording (requires
.BR ffmpeg (1)
on the PATH).
.TP
.BR + ", " =
Add one particle.
.TP
.B \-
Remove one particle.
.TP
.BR Q ", " Esc
Quit.
.PP
Sliders in the stats panel are set by clicking or dragging.  Changes that
affect particle placement (count, radius, curvature, speed, species mix)
reset the simulation.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is plain text,
.RI "one \fIkey\fR = \fIvalue\fR" " per line;"
lines starting with
.B #
are comments.  Keys:
.TP
.BR sim_w ", " sim_h
Simulation area in pixels (200\-2560 \(mu 200\-1440).  The window is 580\ px
wider than
.BR sim_w .
These cannot be changed from the sliders.
.TP
.B n_particles
Starting count (1\-5000; 1\-500 in
.BR ballsim ).
.TP
.B gravity
Downward acceleration in px/s\(S2.
.TP
.B radius
Radius of a light particle in px.  Heavy particles have radius
.IR radius " \(mu " mass_ratio "^(1/3)."
.TP
.B restitution
Coefficient of restitution, 1.0 = elastic.
.TP
.B mono_speed
Speed used by the
.B M
reset; this sets the temperature.
.TP
.B para_a
Parabola curvature.  0 gives a flat rectangular box.
.TP
.BR ceil_amp ", " ceil_freq
Piston amplitude in px (0 = fixed ceiling) and frequency in Hz.  The piston is
quasi-static when
.IR ceil_amp \(mu2\(*p\(mu ceil_freq
is much smaller than
.IR mono_speed ;
faster than that it heats the gas (Fermi acceleration).
.TP
.BR heavy_frac ", " mass_ratio
Fraction of heavy particles and their mass relative to light ones (1\-20).
.TP
.BR substeps ", " passes
Solver settings, as the command-line options.
.SH FILES
Without
.BR \-\-config ,
.B ballsim_v2
uses the first of these that exists:
.PP
.RS
.nf
\&./ballsim_v2.cfg
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ballsim/ballsim_v2.cfg   (~/.config/ballsim/)
$XDG_DATA_HOME/ballsim/ballsim_v2.cfg     (~/.local/share/ballsim/)
\fIDATADIR\fR/ballsim_v2.cfg                    (set at build time)
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B make install
places the pristine default in the share directory.  To customise, copy it to
.I ~/.config/ballsim/
and edit there; it then takes precedence and survives reinstalls.
.B ballsim
(v1) only reads
.I ./ballsim.cfg
or the file given with
.BR \-\-config .
.PP
Recordings are written to the current directory as
.IR ballsim_v2_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS.mp4 .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMP_NUM_THREADS
Thread count, overridden by
.BR \-\-threads .
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_DATA_HOME
Config search directories, see
.BR FILES .
.SH EXAMPLES
Run with defaults:
.PP
.RS
ballsim_v2
.RE
.PP
Create and edit a personal config:
.PP
.RS
.nf
mkdir \-p ~/.config/ballsim
ballsim_v2 \-\-write\-config ~/.config/ballsim/ballsim_v2.cfg
$EDITOR ~/.config/ballsim/ballsim_v2.cfg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Benchmark 2000 particles for 20 simulated seconds with 4 threads:
.PP
.RS
ballsim_v2 \-\-bench 2000 2400 \-\-threads 4 \-\-seed 1
.RE
.PP
Render a frame after 10 s for a README:
.PP
.RS
ballsim_v2 \-\-screenshot frame.bmp 1200 \-\-seed 3
.RE
